<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2015/Rock-Spring1.jpg" alt="Plein air painting at Rock Spring Far" width="400" height="500" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Rock Spring Farm (plein air). 10x8, oil on linen panel. 2015.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Today's paint out was at Rock Spring Farm which is right in the center of Leesburg, VA. &nbsp;It's a great location and there was no shortage of material to paint. so naturally<span style="line-height: 1.42857143;">&nbsp;I settled on painting a window on the old house - I think I just needed a break from the greens for a week or so.</span></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Even though the finished sketch is nearly monochromatic I managed to use a fairly large palette of white, ivory black, ultramarine, burnt sienna, bright red, cad yellow light and yellow ochre. To make things harder I didn't keep enough values back to let me paint highlights on the whites. My workaround was to increase the paint thickness in a few places to catch the light.</p>